<article class="doc">
  <p class="eyebrow">Routing</p>
  <h1>Dynamic routes</h1>
  <p class="lead">A directory segment in brackets is a parameter. <code>routes/posts/[id]/page.sui</code> matches <code>/posts/anything</code>, and the view reads the value as a signal.</p>

  <h2>The [param] segment</h2>
  <p>deck emits a typed pattern — <code>/posts/:id</code> — for any <code>[param]</code> directory. Read the value with <code>route.params.&lt;name&gt;()</code>. It's a signal, so the view re-renders when the parameter changes during client-side navigation.</p>
  <pre class="code">{routeExample}</pre>
  <pre class="code">{readExample}</pre>

  <h2>Try it</h2>
  <p>This site has a live <code>[name]</code> route at <code>routes/examples/greet/[name]/</code>:</p>
  <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/examples/greet/ada">Open /examples/greet/ada →</a></p>

